tients with Secondary Hip Osteoarthritis by Strength Deficit of the Affected Leg.</p></caption><table frame="border" rules="all" width="100%"><thead><tr><th rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Age (Years)</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">BMI (w.h<sup>-2</sup>)</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Comorbidity #</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Gender</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td rowspan="2" align="center" valign="middle" colspan="1">With deficit</td><td rowspan="2" align="center" valign="middle" colspan="1">74.68</td><td rowspan="2" align="center" valign="middle" colspan="1">26.2</td><td rowspan="2" align="center" valign="middle" colspan="1">3.5</td><td align="center" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">35% M</td></tr><tr><td align="center" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">65% F</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="2" align="center" valign="middle" colspan="1">No deficit</td><td rowspan="2" align="center" valign="middle" colspan="1">74.4</td><td rowspan="2" align="center" valign="middle" colspan="1">21.8</td><td rowspan="2" align="center" valign="middle" colspan="1">1.35</td><td align="center" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">40% M</td></tr><tr><td align="center" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">60% F</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="T3FN1"><p>BMI=body mass index; F=female; M=male; #=number.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>